// Copy this file to Secrets.xcconfig (same directory) and fill in your own
// values. Secrets.xcconfig is gitignored - it never gets committed.
// Config.xcconfig includes it automatically if present.
//
//     cp Secrets.xcconfig.example Secrets.xcconfig
//
// Every setting here is optional. With no Secrets.xcconfig at all the app
// still builds and runs in the simulator; only the features that need a
// value are affected.


// --- Signing -------------------------------------------------------------
// Your 10-character Apple Development Team ID. Required only to run on a
// physical device; simulator builds don't need it. Find it in Xcode under
// Settings -> Accounts -> your Apple ID -> Team ID, or at
// https://developer.apple.com/account (Membership details).
// LOCAL_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345

// Appended to the bundle identifier, which defaults to com.Fridge.FridgeFit.
// Leave this unset unless device installs fail with a provisioning error -
// that happens when your Apple ID can't claim the default id. A suffix like
// ".yourname" gives you com.Fridge.FridgeFit.yourname.
//
// Note: the committed GoogleService-Info.plist is registered against
// com.Fridge.FridgeFit. Firebase logs a bundle-id mismatch warning with a
// suffix set but keeps working, and Google Sign-In is unaffected because it
// keys off CLIENT_ID. See README "Bundle Identifier".
// LOCAL_BUNDLE_ID_SUFFIX = .yourname


// --- Ingredient substitutions --------------------------------------------
// Nothing to configure. Substitutions are generated on-device by Apple
// Intelligence, so there is no API key and no account - see the README.
// The feature needs an Apple Intelligence capable device with the feature
// turned on; where it isn't available, "Find Substitute" says so.


// --- TURN relay (remote camera, optional) --------------------------------
// The remote-camera prototype uses Google's public STUN servers by default,
// which costs nothing and needs no account. STUN is enough when both iPhones
// can reach each other directly - same Wi-Fi, usually - but it does NOT
// relay traffic, so a connection across different networks (one device on
// cellular, or either behind carrier-grade NAT) can fail outright.
//
// A TURN server fixes that by relaying. None is required to run or test the
// prototype, and FridgeFit does not ship or pay for one. Set all three of
// these to use your own; leave them unset and the app runs STUN-only and
// says so on screen.
//
// TURN_URL = turn:turn.example.com:3478
// TURN_USERNAME = your-turn-username
// TURN_CREDENTIAL = your-turn-password


// --- Spoonacular (Discover tab: online recipes, NOT YET ACTIVE) ----------
// Online recipe search is switched OFF in code and does not need a key to
// build, launch, or pass its tests. Setting a key here is step 1 of 3 and
// on its own changes nothing.
//
// To enable online search:
//   1. Get a key at https://spoonacular.com/food-api/console#Dashboard and
//      uncomment the line below. This file is the template; your real values
//      belong in Secrets.xcconfig, which is gitignored. Never commit a key.
//   2. In FridgeFit/Data/OnlineRecipeFeature.swift, change
//      `provider` from `.disabled` to `.enabled`.
//   3. Rebuild. A missing or malformed key is reported on screen as
//      "not configured" rather than failing, so there is nothing else to do.
//
// Saving recipes from Discover is a separate switch with its own
// prerequisite - the savedRecipes Firestore rules must be deployed first.
// See `savedRecipeStorage` in the same file.
//
// Note a key placed in an iOS app bundle is extractable from the shipped
// binary; a backend proxy is the only way to keep it private in production.
//
// SPOONACULAR_API_KEY = your-spoonacular-api-key-here
